   "etymology": "From Proto-Albanian *duk-, from Proto-Indo-European *dewk- (“to draw”). An etymological connection to ancient Greek δοκέω and Gothic þugkjan (to think, to appear) is phonetically impossible. The use of third-person singular present of δοκέω, δοκεῖ (\"it seems\" [to me]) in ancient Greek probably influenced its use in the form më duket (it seems to me) in Albanian.",
